Portions of this software (the number-format grammar, the value-to-string
rendering algorithms, the built-in format table, and the associated edge-case
handling) are ported from ssf v0.11.2 and remain under the Apache License,
Version 2.0.

Changes made in this port relative to the upstream JavaScript source:

  - Translated from JavaScript to Rust.
  - Calendar dates are derived from the date serial via pure civil-date
    arithmetic rather than the host `Date` object, making results deterministic
    and independent of the host timezone/DST.
  - The public formatting entry points return `Result` values instead of
    throwing on unsupported/invalid input.

Folio modifications (2026-09-19):
  - Exposed section selection for display colors and layout directives.
  - Rounded date/time fields together to carry seconds through midnight.
  - Returned an error for oversized fixed fraction denominators.

Folio modifications (0.35):
  - Added bounded format-shape validation and TEXT numeric formatting shared
    by the formula engine and cell renderer.

Folio modifications (Office corpus, 2026-09-25):
  - `a/p` keeps the case of the format's letters ("a"/"p" or "A"/"P"), as
    Excel does.
  - A single `s` before a fractional-seconds token prints whole seconds;
    the fraction was printed twice (`h:m:s.00` gave "4:5:6.01.01").

Folio modifications (Excel-correct results part 2, 2026-09-26):
  - Number sections are rendered by `excelnum.rs` from their placeholders
    (digit placeholders, grouping and scaling commas, percent, fractions and
    scientific notation with literal text anywhere) instead of `ssf`'s list
    of recognized shapes. `000.00` keeps its leading zero.
  - Any character outside the format syntax is shown as itself.
  - A single conditional section applies only when its condition holds;
    other values show as General. Conditions may contain spaces.
  - `@` inside quotes doesn't make a section the text section.
  - `[h]` or `[s]` makes a plain `h` or `s` show the elapsed total; negative
    elapsed times show as `-` and their length; `m` after seconds is minutes.
  - `checked::text` formats text (and TRUE/FALSE) through the text section.
  - tests/text_format_cases.rs: 832 TEXT rows from Apache POI's format test
    workbooks with Excel's results, all matching.
